---
import ContentPage from '../components/ContentPage.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
import { content } from '../i18n/content';

const title = 'AI Search Visibility: GEO, AEO and AIO Systems | Teyfik Gökdemir';
const description = 'A practical system for making businesses understandable, discoverable and reference-ready across search engines, answer engines and AI-assisted discovery.';
const pathname = '/ai-search-visibility/';
const canonical = site.origin + pathname;

const faq = [
  {
    question: 'What is AI search visibility?',
    answer: 'AI search visibility is the ability of a person, business or brand to be discovered, understood and accurately represented by search engines, answer engines and AI-assisted research systems.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Is GEO different from SEO?',
    answer: 'Yes. SEO focuses primarily on discoverability and ranking in traditional search results. GEO focuses on making information clear, attributable and useful for generative systems that synthesise answers.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Does llms.txt guarantee AI citations?',
    answer: 'No. An llms.txt file may provide useful machine-readable context, but it does not guarantee indexing, citations or rankings. Strong public content, clear entities, technical accessibility and reliable evidence remain more important.',
  },
  {
    question: 'How long does AI visibility work take?',
    answer: 'Technical corrections can be implemented quickly, but recognition and citation depend on crawling, indexing, content quality, external references and the consistency of the entity over time.',
  },
];

const pageSchema = {
  '@type': ['WebPage', 'FAQPage'],
  '@id': canonical + '#webpage',
  url: canonical,
  name: title,
  description,
  inLanguage: 'en',
  isPartOf: { '@id': site.origin + '/#website' },
  about: [
    'Generative Engine Optimization',
    'Answer Engine Optimization',
    'AI Optimization',
    'Search Engine Optimization',
  ],
  mainEntity: faq.map((item) => ({
    '@type': 'Question',
    name: item.question,
    acceptedAnswer: {
      '@type': 'Answer',
      text: item.answer,
    },
  })),
};

const alternates = {
  en: site.origin + '/ai-search-visibility/',
  ru: site.origin + '/ru/ai-search-visibility/',
  tr: site.origin + '/yapay-zeka-arama-gorunurlugu/',
  sq: site.origin + '/sq/dukshmeria-ne-kerkimin-ai/',
  mk: site.origin + '/mk/vidlivost-vo-ai-prebaruvanje/',
  sr: site.origin + '/sr/vidljivost-u-ai-pretrazi/',
  fa: site.origin + '/fa/مشاهده-پذیری-در-جستجوی-هوش-مصنوعی/',
  zh: site.origin + '/zh/ai-search-visibility/',
  'x-default': site.origin + '/ai-search-visibility/',
};
---
<ContentPage
  locale="en"
  title={title}
  description={description}
  pathname={pathname}
  alternates={alternates}
  pageSchema={pageSchema}
  eyebrow="AI Search Visibility"
  heading="Make your business understandable to search engines and AI systems."
  lead="A structured visibility system connecting technical SEO, entity clarity, answer-ready content, evidence and machine-readable information."
>
  <div class="answer-block">
    <p><strong>AI search visibility</strong> is not a separate trick or a single file. It is the result of building a technically accessible, clearly defined and evidence-supported digital presence that both people and machines can understand.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>What the system covers</h2>

  <div class="content-grid">
    <article class="content-card">
      <h3>Technical discovery</h3>
      <p>Canonical URLs, crawl access, sitemaps, language targeting, performance and structured data.</p>
    </article>

    <article class="content-card">
      <h3>Entity clarity</h3>
      <p>Consistent identity, expertise, ventures, profiles, relationships and authoritative source pages.</p>
    </article>

    <article class="content-card">
      <h3>Answer-ready content</h3>
      <p>Direct explanations, useful definitions, visible questions and structured information architecture.</p>
    </article>

    <article class="content-card">
      <h3>Evidence and attribution</h3>
      <p>Claims supported by observable work, reliable references, case studies and consistent public information.</p>
    </article>
  </div>

  <h2>SEO, GEO, AEO and AIO work together</h2>

  <p><strong>SEO</strong> creates the technical and content foundation for search discovery. <strong>GEO</strong> improves how information can be interpreted and referenced by generative systems. <strong>AEO</strong> structures content around clear answers. <strong>AIO</strong> connects the wider website, entity and content system for AI-assisted discovery.</p>

  <p>These disciplines should not be treated as four unrelated services. The strongest implementation begins with one coherent information architecture and applies each discipline where it creates measurable value.</p>

  <h2>How I approach AI search visibility</h2>

  <ol>
    <li><strong>Audit discovery:</strong> crawl access, canonical signals, indexing, language structure and technical conflicts.</li>
    <li><strong>Define the entity:</strong> establish who the business is, what it does, where it operates and how its properties relate.</li>
    <li><strong>Map commercial questions:</strong> identify the questions prospects, search engines and research systems need answered.</li>
    <li><strong>Create source pages:</strong> publish deep, focused pages that can function as reliable reference points.</li>
    <li><strong>Add structured data:</strong> represent visible information accurately without manufacturing claims.</li>
    <li><strong>Strengthen evidence:</strong> connect expertise to projects, outcomes, public profiles and trusted external mentions.</li>
    <li><strong>Measure discovery:</strong> monitor search impressions, branded queries, referrals and observable citation patterns.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>What this work does not promise</h2>

  <p>No responsible consultant can guarantee that ChatGPT, Google, Perplexity, Claude or another system will cite a specific page. Each system controls its own crawling, indexing, retrieval and answer-generation processes.</p>

  <p>The goal is to remove technical barriers, increase clarity, create useful source material and improve the probability that the business is discovered and represented accurately.</p>

  <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>

  <div class="faq-list">
    {faq.map((item) => (
      <details>
        <summary>{item.question}</summary>
        <p>{item.answer}</p>
      </details>
    ))}
  </div>

  <section class="content-cta">
    <h2>Build a stronger search and AI discovery system.</h2>
    <p>For an audit or implementation project, contact <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> or review the <a href="/blog/seo-vs-geo-vs-aeo-vs-aio/">SEO, GEO, AEO and AIO guide</a>.</p>
  </section>
</ContentPage>